      "@type": "FAQPage",
      mainEntity: [
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "Can you seal old concrete?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "Yes, and old concrete is often a better candidate than new. Cured concrete has finished the bulk of its shrinkage and its surface is open and porous, so a penetrating sealer soaks in readily. The conditions are that the slab is structurally sound, thoroughly clean, free of any previous sealer that would block absorption, and properly dry before the product goes on.",
          },
